# Harmony AI App Tech Context
@Core: React Native 0.86.0, TypeScript, React Navigation (Native Stack), React Native Paper (MD3).
@State: React Hooks (current), Context API (theme/auth/emoji), Redux/Zustand (future complex state).
@Data: embedded Soulbits Engine over its loopback management REST API (NO app-side SQLite replica since 3-4; the repository seam `src/database/repositories/index.ts` re-exports the API-backed adapters in `src/services/engine/repositories/*`), AsyncStorage (settings/preferences), React Native Keychain / Android Keystore (secrets + engine DB key).
@Sync: engine↔engine **changeset-v1** (SQLite session-extension changesets) — implemented ENGINE-SIDE; the app does NOT speak the sync protocol. The app configures it through the engine's sync-client REST surface via `DesktopSyncScreen` (`src/screens/settings/DesktopSyncScreen.tsx`): live reconfigure/status/authority hand-over. The desktop engine is the write authority; the embedded engine yields and buffers (buffer-and-forward). The retired app-side rows-v1 stack (SyncService, per-source watermarks `last_sync_timestamp:*`, name-clash resolution, size-estimate confirm, wipe/rebuild) was deleted in 3-4. The engine advertises `sync_schema_version` (3) + `sync_protocol: ["changeset-v1"]` as a mismatched-dev-builds guard.
@Network: loopback HTTP/WS to the embedded engine (management REST + event WebSocket on 127.0.0.1); Axios for outbound inference/cloud calls; engine↔engine changeset-v1 over LAN (engine-side).
@Build: Metro Bundler, Gradle 8.13 (NOT 9.0+), Android SDK API 24-33, JDK 17.
@BuildFlavors: react-native-config@1.6.1 wired into src/config/cloud.ts; IS_BETA coercion (=== true || === 'true'). Android productFlavors dev/prod (buildConfigField, applicationIdSuffix ".dev"). iOS CI-driven (env regeneration + PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER override). google-services plugin 4.4.2. OAuth secrets: scripts/oauth-secrets.cjs reads gitignored client_secret_*.json per env → generates .env + android/gradle-secrets.<flavor>.properties (both gitignored). Resolve priority: -P flag > gradle-secrets file > ''. cloud.ts exports APP_ENV/APP_ENVIRONMENT (env: dev|prod, label). CI uses vars.GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID / vars.APPLE_SERVICES_ID.
@Dev Tools: TypeScript compiler, ESLint, Prettier, Jest, React Native Debugger, hot reload. `test:unit` runs with `--maxWorkers=40` (must be >= number of unit test files — 35 — or the documented better-sqlite3 cross-worker contamination intermittently fails UNIQUE/FK/rollback tests).
@Future Integrations:
- On-Device AI: React Native Executorch (PyTorch models, quantized up to 7B)
- Audio: React Native Voice (STT), React Native TTS
- Media: Image Picker, Camera, FFmpeg
- Services: biometric auth, cloud backup (FCM push is now integrated in-app — see @Key Deps)
@APIs: embedded Soulbits Engine management REST (`/api/entities/*`, `/api/messages/*`, `/api/character-profiles/*`, `/api/module-configs/*`, `/api/providers` + `/api/providers/verify` + `/api/providers/models` + `/api/providers/capabilities` — shared accounts CRUD, stateless key verification, live model/voice listing, embedded capability catalog; management contract **1.6.0** since v0.4.5, `/api/stats/*`, `/api/backup/*`, `/api/sync/client/*`) + engine event WebSocket — all over loopback (`X-Loopback-Token`).
@Performance: Lazy loading, image optimization, FlatList virtualization, memoization, code splitting, JOIN-based queries for chat list previews.
@Security: EncryptedStorage, HTTPS, token auth, SSL pinning (consideration), no plaintext credentials.
@Platforms: Android 7.0+ (API 24), target API 33.
@Workflow: Local dev → emulator/ADB testing → release builds → Play Store (future). `npm run android` now auto-provisions the embedded engine (`preandroid` → `scripts/build-engine-sidecar.cjs`) and starts Metro (no separate `npm start`); engine repo via `SOULBITS_ENGINE_REPO` (default sibling `../harmony-link-private`), `ENGINE_SIDECAR_REBUILD=1` forces a rebuild.
@Key Deps: react 19.2.7, react-native 0.86.0, @react-navigation/*  ^7.x, react-native-paper ^5.x, @react-native-async-storage/async-storage ^2.x, eventemitter3 ^5.x, uuid ^13.x, music-metadata v11, react-native-device-info, @harmony-ai-solutions/soulbits-api-client (GitHub git dep). **Dropped in 3-4:** react-native-sqlite-storage, react-native-restart, better-sqlite3 (+ @types). **Embedded engine (not npm):** `libengine.so` (Android, vendored per ABI) / `SoulbitsEngine.xcframework` (iOS). **Firebase (7-12):** `@react-native-firebase/app` + `@react-native-firebase/messaging` ^26.4.0 (modular API; runtime-guarded, placeholder `google-services.json` / `GoogleService-Info.plist` shipped — SDK token takes precedence over the native raw-APNs seam via `PushTokenStore`).
@ModularConfig:
- Provider configuration is ACCOUNT-BASED (v0.4.5 provider-registry workstream): shared `provider_accounts` (credentials) + per-module `capability_json` overlays, managed over the engine accounts API. The per-module `provider_config_*` tables/columns, the 6-1 interim `legacyProviderAdapter`, and the 2-1 interim `providerModelCatalog.ts` constant are DELETED.
- `accountFieldSchemas.ts`: per-type ACCOUNT form fields (name; api_key required-ness per type; base_url required/optional/managed; extras — openai org+project, xai team, comfyui auth + comfyui_mode read-only engine-persisted, soulbitscloud auth-mode). Drives the shared `AccountForm` + Providers screen. `providerFieldSchemas.ts` is capability-only (feeds the module-config capability section).
- `moduleConfiguration.ts`: module type definitions + per-module provider options — mistral/ollama/localai reactivated (ollama STT experimental per R-AUDIO); STT has PER-SLOT provider lists (transcription ≠ VAD; VAD = soulbitscloud + soulvoice only). `moduleDefaults.ts` retains the form-defaults role.
- Module-config form flow (ModuleConfigEditScreen): Provider → Account (auto-collapses when single; "Add account…" opens AccountForm) → Capability → Module; STT keeps dual transcription/VAD sub-forms. Model pickers are catalog-backed (`getProviderCapabilities`, offline-first) with on-demand "Fetch from provider" (`listProviderModels`, module filter engine-side; voices envelope for ElevenLabs), provenance chips (detected/known/assumed) + Custom… free-text fallback; param warnings never hard-block. Account switch revalidates overlay model/voice refs (stale marked, never dropped).
- Sampling presets: `usePresets` + `SamplingPresetSelect` in the capability section (A3 semantics — presets supply defaults, explicit local values override; sampling_preset_name + extra_params columns, migration 021; extra params = JSON TEXT key-value pairs).
- Cloud engine credential (2026-10-23 incident): the soulbitscloud ACCOUNT api_key is a long-lived `sb_cloud_*` API key named "Soulbits Engine", ensured (reuse-or-mint) and written only when changed by `engineKeyEnsure`; `soulbitsTokenSync` / iOS wake seams / `seeding` drive that flow instead of pushing the PASETO. Signed out = nothing written. The relay token keeps its own PASETO recovery machinery (unchanged).
- Soulbits model catalog: `soulbitsModelsCatalog.ts` + `SoulbitsModelSelect` remain for soulbitscloud pickers (live `GET /v1/models`, credential-less, 5-min TTL, never throws → static fallback); general model pickers now use the engine capabilities endpoint instead.
- Beta release build: `cd android; .\gradlew.bat assembleDevRelease -PE2E_DEBUG_SIGNING=true` → `app\build\outputs\apk\dev\release\app-dev-release.apk` (JS-bundled, debug-signed; only debug.keystore exists locally). Install: `adb -s d608825c install -r <apk>`.
@Phase09-LifecycleUI:
- Soulbits Engine management UI adds Lifecycle Settings tab to character profile
- Exposes lifecycle_config fields for per-entity autonomy configuration
- Not directly synced to app (app receives emotion state via sync, not lifecycle config)
- App's autonomy behavior controlled locally, not via Soulbits Engine lifecycle settings
@Interactions:
- DB: interactions table with entity_id, interaction_scope, participant_key, participant_ids, status, presence_type, summary, memory_id, continued_interaction_id
- Migrations 24-28 sequentially applied: create_interactions, drop_session_id, add_summary, memory_lifecycle_fields, add_presence_type
- Repository: interactions.ts with CRUD, participant key derivation, scope derivation, JOIN-based chat list queries
- Participant key derivation: sorted entity ID pair join for private, sorted full set join for group, empty string for world
- Chat list query pattern: JOIN conversation_messages + interactions for single-round-trip last message preview, two-phase TEXT column loading for large audio/image data
@Emoji:
- Emoji Sets: native (platform default), twemoji (Twitter 64px sprite), noto (Google 64px sprite) — bundled as PNG spritesheets in src/assets/emoji/sheets/
- Emoji Data: Pre-built category-organized data (src/services/EmojiService.ts), keyword-based search, skin tone variants (5 modifiers)
- DB: emoji_actions table (migrations 22-23) with per-entity emoji → action mappings, emotion_effects JSON column, cooldown_seconds, soft delete via deleted_at
- Emotion model: Ekman8 base emotions (joy, sadness, trust, disgust, fear, anger, surprise, anticipation) with signed delta intensity (-5.0 to +5.0)
- AdditionalEffects payload: { emotionEffects: EmotionEffect[] } — packaged per SEND_MESSAGE via EmojiService.resolveMessageActions()
- EmojiAwareText: Segments text into emoji/text spans using regex; EmojiText renders with sprite caching
- Context: EmojiContext (style preferences, set selection, skin tone), EmojiProvider wraps app root
